          {
            "row": 2,
            "before": "The NBRC1321 cyanocobalamin stock and the JCM403 generic B12 comparison concern a W07 stock. The existing W05 thiamine403 stock is a different solute and is not implicated by name or medium number alone. No B12 owner is created or changed here.",
            "after": "The NBRC1321 cyanocobalamin stock is W08 frozen entry 747. Its source explicitly names cyanocobalamin, while the JCM403 generic B12 comparison remains unresolved as a possible same preparation. The existing W05 thiamine403 stock is a different solute and is not implicated by name or medium number alone. No B12 owner is created or changed here.",
            "review": "PASS: actual frozen author/source/material scopes restored; original source_disposition, IDs and all other objects unchanged."
          },
          {
            "row": 8,
            "before": "W05 Polypeptone already uses a generic local identity and rejects the three unsupported Hipolypepton product aliases. Bare historical labels do not establish a BD/Japanese product. The competing W08 whole-owner proposal requires coordinator reconciliation; this audit chooses no winner and does not merge its history into W05.",
            "after": "W05 Polypeptone already uses a generic local identity and rejects the three unsupported Hipolypepton product aliases. Bare historical labels do not establish a BD/Japanese product. The competing W06 whole-owner proposal, frozen entry 540, requires coordinator reconciliation; this audit chooses no winner and does not merge its history into W05.",
            "review": "PASS: actual frozen author/source/material scopes restored; original source_disposition, IDs and all other objects unchanged."
          },
          {
            "row": 11,
            "before": "Hutner JCM932/JCM1464/NBRC589 union is parent-authored. The 3.335/3.34 g calcium notation can retain rounded and literal forms while malformed molybdate remains ungrounded. COMPLETE means the immediate source list, not complete molecular identity. This audit does not duplicate that union.",
            "after": "The Hutner DSMZ590/1144 union is parent-authored. The source comparison supports one nominal preparation while retaining both 3.335/3.34 g calcium literals, the nested Metals44 list, pH7 to6.8 adjustment, approximately7.3 g KOH, and NaOH-or-H2SO4 details. Historical malformed molybdate literals remain ungrounded; they do not establish alternative chemical identities. COMPLETE refers to the immediate source list, not complete molecular grounding. Comparison to JCM900/979 remains separately unresolved. This audit does not duplicate that union.",
            "review": "PASS: actual frozen author/source/material scopes restored; original source_disposition, IDs and all other objects unchanged."
          },
          {
            "row": 20,
            "before": "W10 calf-blood provenance must preserve blood rather than mistakenly say serum, as current comment 6719103915 clarifies. Calf age does not establish defibrination or whole-blood processing. No W05 selected candidate is this source.",
            "after": "The W10 JCM1303 heat-inactivated calf-serum proposal shares MediaDive2061 source continuity with the existing Bovine_Calf_Serum owner. Reconcile that continuity and the broader/Gibco occurrences before adding or narrowing an owner; omitted heat metadata or a new filename does not establish a different material. No W05 selected candidate is this source. The calf-blood wording issue in comment6719103915 concerns a separate TOGO M2854 proposal and remains in the distinct additional-comment disposition.",
            "review": "PASS: actual frozen author/source/material scopes restored; original source_disposition, IDs and all other objects unchanged."
          }
        ],
        "original_primary_seal_and_all40files_unchanged": true
      }
